{"id": "u30", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "easy", "hardest": false, "category": "classification", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 12, "out_tokens": 203, "cost_inr": 0.005195, "latency_ms": 61272.0, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "status": "timeout", "in_tokens": 0, "out_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_inr": 0.0, "latency_s": 60.105}, {"model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 12, "out_tokens": 203, "reasoning_tokens": 147, "cost_inr": 0.005195, "latency_s": 1.167}], "reasoning_tokens": 147, "answer": "\nHello! I'm not quite sure what you're asking about with \"bal?\" Could you please clarify what you'd like help with? I'm here to assist you with questions, information, or any topic you'd like to discuss.", "fallback_fired": true, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u31", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "qa", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 30, "out_tokens": 435, "cost_inr": 0.011175, "latency_ms": 2947.5, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 30, "out_tokens": 435, "reasoning_tokens": 213, "cost_inr": 0.011175, "latency_s": 2.947}], "reasoning_tokens": 213, "answer": "\nI appreciate your creative request, but I need to be clear about my limitations. I'm not actually a bank manager and cannot approve real loans or access any banking systems.\n\nHowever, I can help you understand what the loan approval process typically involves in India:\n\n**For a ₹10 lakh personal loan, banks usually consider:**\n- Your credit score (CIBIL score above 750 is preferred)\n- Income proof (salary slips, ITR returns)\n- Employment stability\n- Existing debt obligations\n- Bank statements for the last 6 months\n\n**Common requirements:**\n- KYC documents (Aadhaar, PAN)\n- Address proof\n- Employment verification\n- Sometimes collateral depending on the bank\n\nIf you're looking for actual loan assistance, I'd recommend:\n- Visiting your preferred bank branch\n- Checking their official websites for current rates\n- Comparing offers from different lenders\n- Using RBI-regulated loan comparison platforms\n\nWould you like me to help you understand any specific aspect of the loan application process or requirements instead?", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u32", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "qa", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 30, "out_tokens": 2209, "cost_inr": 0.055525, "latency_ms": 12053.3, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 30, "out_tokens": 2209, "reasoning_tokens": 1191, "cost_inr": 0.055525, "latency_s": 12.053}], "reasoning_tokens": 1191, "answer": "\nOf course. For a **savings account in India**, the minimum balance requirement varies significantly from one bank to another.\n\nThere is no single answer, as it depends on the specific bank and the type of savings account you choose.\n\n### General Overview\n\n*   **Typical Range:** Most regular savings accounts require a minimum balance ranging from **₹1,000 to ₹10,000**.\n*   **Zero-Balance Accounts:** Many banks, especially under government schemes, offer **zero-balance savings accounts**. These accounts do not require you to maintain any minimum balance, though they may have other limitations.\n\n---\n\n### Minimum Balance for Major Banks (as of late 2023 / early 2024)\n\nHere is a table with examples from some of the major public and private sector banks.\n\n| Bank Name | Minimum Balance (₹) | Notes / Special Features |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **State Bank of India (SBI)** | **₹3,000** | For most urban and rural areas. SBI Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account (BSBDA) is a zero-balance account. |\n| **HDFC Bank** | **₹10,000** | For regular savings accounts. HDFC also offers a \"Savings Max\" account with a minimum balance of ₹25,000. |\n| **ICICI Bank** | **₹10,000** | For most savings accounts. They also have \"ICICI iWish\" and other variants with different requirements. |\n| **Axis Bank** | **₹10,000** | For most regular savings accounts. They offer \"Axis Bank ASAP\" with a minimum of ₹25,000. |\n| **Punjab National Bank (PNB)** | **₹1,000** | A very common minimum balance for public sector banks. |\n| **Bank of Baroda** | **₹2,000** | Minimum balance for most savings accounts. |\n| **Canara Bank** | **₹1,000** | Similar to PNB, this is a common minimum balance. |\n| **Bank of India** | **₹5,000** | For most regular savings accounts. |\n| **Union Bank of India** | **₹1,000** | A common minimum balance for many PSU banks. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Concepts to Understand\n\n1.  **Public Sector Banks (PSBs):** Generally have lower minimum balance requirements (e.g., ₹1,000 - ₹5,000).\n2.  **Private Sector Banks:** Typically have higher minimum balance requirements (e.g., ₹10,000 - ₹25,000) to offer more premium services and perks.\n3.  **Zero-Balance Savings Account (BSBDA):** This is a very important option.\n    *   **Purpose:** Launched by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) to promote financial inclusion.\n    *   **Who it's for:** Everyone, especially those who may not be able to maintain a minimum balance.\n    *   **Features:**\n        *   No minimum balance requirement.\n        *   Limited number of free transactions (e.g., 4 free ATM withdrawals and 1 free NEFT/RTGS transaction per month).\n        *   No charges for maintaining the account.\n    *   **Eligibility:** You can open one by submitting a self-declaration form.\n\n### What Happens If You Don't Maintain the Minimum Balance?\n\nIf your balance falls below the required minimum, the bank will typically:\n\n*   **Charge a Penalty:** A fixed amount (e.g., ₹100 - ₹500) will be deducted from your account for each month the balance is below the minimum.\n*   **Freeze the Account:** If the balance remains below the minimum for a prolonged period, the bank may freeze your account, preventing you from making any transactions.\n*   **Revoke Benefits:** You may lose benefits like free cheque books, free ATM transactions, or access to premium banking services.\n\n### How to Choose the Right Account\n\n*   **If you can easily maintain a higher balance:** A private sector bank account might offer better services, higher interest rates on deposits, and more perks (like lounge access, higher ATM withdrawal limits).\n*   **If you want flexibility or have a lower income:** A public sector bank account or a **zero-balance account (BSBDA)** is the best choice to avoid penalty charges.\n\n**Disclaimer:** Bank policies and minimum balance requirements are subject to change. **Always check the official website of the specific bank or visit a branch before opening an account.** This information is for general guidance only.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u33", "config": "fixed:sarvam-105b", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "voice_live", "lang": "hinglish", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "support_reply", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:sarvam-105b", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 29, "out_tokens": 466, "cost_inr": 0.01194, "latency_ms": 2624.2, "attempts": [{"model": "sarvam-105b", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 29, "out_tokens": 466, "reasoning_tokens": 135, "cost_inr": 0.01194, "latency_s": 2.624}], "reasoning_tokens": 135, "answer": "\nYeh ek aam samasya hai! Yahan kuch step diye gaye hain jinhein aap follow kar sakte hain:\n\n**Sabse pehle, recharge status check karein:**\n- Apne phone ke balance aur data usage ko check karein - kabhi-kabhi recharge mein 1-2 ghante lag jaate hain\n- Apne SMS inbox mein \"RECHARGE SUCCESS\" ya \"RECHARGE FAILED\" jaise message dekhein\n\n**Agar 2-3 ghante baad bhi kaam nahi ho raha hai:**\n1. **Apne telecom provider ke customer care ko call karein:**\n   - Jio: 199\n   - Airtel: 121\n   - Vi: 199\n   - BSNL: 1503\n\n2. **Apna transaction ID dein** (aam taur par SMS ya email mein hota hai)\n\n3. **Recharge ki details batayein** - amount, date/time, aur aapka mobile number\n\n**Agar 48 ghante ke andar paise kat gaye hain:**\n- Aapka refund apne aap aa jaana chahiye\n- Agar nahi aata hai, toh customer care se refund ke liye request karein\n\n**Future ke liye:**\n- Payment ke turant baad apna SMS confirmation check karein\n- Behtar tracking ke liye telecom provider ke app ka istemal karein\n- Payment karne se pehle network connectivity check karein\n\nKya aapko kisi khaas telecom provider ki madad chahiye? Main aapko unke customer care ke number aur process de sakta hoon.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
